# React components in features

## One export per file

App components under `src/features/` export a single component. Private helpers (e.g. `getBarColorClassName`) may stay in the same file.

## Subcomponents

If a file grows multiple React components, extract them to sibling files in the same `components/` folder:

```tsx
// skills-content.tsx — orchestrator
import { SkillBar } from "./skill-bar";

// experience-content.tsx — orchestrator
import { TechIcon } from "./tech-icon";
import { ExperienceCompanyIcon } from "./experience-company-icon";
```

## Portfolio data vs i18n

- Structure (projects, tech, achievements keys, URLs): `src/features/shared/lib/portfolio-data.ts`
- User-facing text (ES/EN): `src/features/shared/lib/locales/{es,en}/common.json`
- Types: `src/features/shared/types/dictionaries.ts`

## React patterns

- Hoist static maps and JSX nodes at module level, not inside render functions.
- Use stable keys in `.map()` (`project.name`, `achievement`, `tech`), not array indices.
- Prefer `"use client"` only where hooks or interactivity are needed.
